      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just \"possible\" though. i can literally feel it. like, my brother sent me a message yesterday that used a specific emoji combo i never use, but it was placed exactly where i usually put an emphasis point. it felt like seeing a stranger wearing my skin. if you guys are actually capable of scraping way more than just public posts—like if you can actually map the psychological \"why\" behind how i talk—how would i even prove it's me and not the model? like, what would a \"replica\" be missing that i can look for?",
